{
	"_note": "Kajika-yu, the hot spring in its clearing in the wood west of Kajika Gorge (2026-11-24, after the user's photo of a forest onsen: the pool the heart of the view, shut in by green woods, mist lying over the water, big mossy rocks standing in it, lanterns in the trees; docs/DESIGN.md → ที่อาบน้ำ). On the valley's plan at [-60, 6], its east edge meeting the gorge's west edge (the path in at rows 18-19 here, rows 4-5 there). The pool fills the clearing's middle (rows 4-11, about 13 x 8): the clearing's floor moss (legend `m`, tile `moss`: no lawn under the trees), the map's water of look `onsen` (legend `o`: milky turquoise, a soft stony shore sloping down, PondShape; the steam lying on it all day, MistRules `onsen`), mossy boulders standing in it (garden_rock `boulder`) and on its banks, the `onsen` prop over it naming the bath (no look of its own; \"seats\": \"shore\": in from any open dry cell beside its water, Game.soak_spots; data/baths.json kajika, open 16:00-02:00). The wood is thick behind it (north and west, where the play camera looks) and lighter toward the eye; past the edges a broadleaf wood (data/vista.json apron_trees). Five stone lanterns in the trees round the water, a cypress bucket with a towel at its south shore (`oke`), the changing hut at the back of the clearing in the trees, past the water (`bath_hut`, \"use\": \"change\": into a towel and back, Game.change_clothes; `towel` allowed here, the way out only dressed) beside a bamboo screen (where the photo's lit building stands; never between the eye and the water), reached on open grass round the pool's west side (column 2, row 13 kept free; the user could not walk to it); a bamboo stand in the back corner, the wood's trees of mixed sizes, and wild undergrowth (shrub `wild`: three or four rough mounds heaped, never flowering) along the shore and under the trees instead of clipped garden shrubs. Under the wood's canopy (`shade`: the sun dimmed, the picture greener, the leaves' dappled shadows on the ground and water: Game.shade_tint / shade_sun, DappleRules; shafts of sun slanting through the steam at `shafts` `at`, brightest at the low sun of morning and late afternoon: LightShafts, 3D only; the user wanted it shadier, 2026-11-25), big maples reaching over the back shore too. Sat in the water the camera comes down low across it (data/vista.json kajika_soak). Format: README.md, Maps. A bamboo spout (kakehi, 2026-11-28) on the east bank at [14, 5] pours the spring's water in toward the middle (Kakehi): its stream, foam, rings and sound. Ferns in the rocks' crevices round the shore (2026-11-28; none on the west bank by the boulder, where the user saw them as green spikes). A name board by the path in at [10, 17], a plank bench beside the changing house at [6, 2] and its buckets stacked behind it at [6, 1].",
